window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Linear Algebra", "projects": [{"id": "LA-01", "slug": "ranknullity-theorem", "title": "Rank–Nullity Theorem", "target": "<p>For a linear map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith finite-dimensional\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim V=\\dim\\ker T+\\dim\\operatorname{im}T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>All vector spaces are over one field F. V is finite-dimensional; W\nneed not be. Import basis extension in a finite-dimensional vector\nspace, and the definitions of kernel, image, linear independence, and\nspan. The zero-dimensional cases use an empty basis.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Extend a kernel basis", "proof": "1. Choose a basis u₁,…,u_k ofkerT and extend it to u₁,…,u_k,v₁,…,v_r ofV.\n\n2. Thus dimV=k+r.\n\n3. For any x∈V write x=∑a_i u_i+∑b_j v_j.\n\n4. ApplyingT yields Tx=∑b_jTv_j because every u_i lies in the kernel.\n\n5. Hence the vectorsTv_j spanimT.", "role": "<p>Complete the basis in the domain, not the codomain.</p>", "inputs": "<p>T linear;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nbasis of kerT; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The images\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_{1},\\ldots ,Tv_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nspan the image.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The images\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_{1},\\ldots ,Tv_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nspan the image.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain T linear;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nbasis of kerT; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions\nand versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Complete the basis in the domain, not the codomain.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The added basis vectors must complement the whole kernel.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Choose a basis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nof ker T and extend it to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k,v_{1},\\ldots ,v_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nof V.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{dim} V=k+r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in V</annotation></semantics></math>\nwrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=\\sum a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i+\\sum b_j</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>ApplyingT yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tx=\\sum b_jTv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in the kernel.</p>", "<p>Hence the vectors\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nspan im T.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>The added basis vectors must complement the whole kernel. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: The added basis vectors must\ncomplement the whole kernel. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Image independence and dimension", "proof": "1. If∑b_jTv_j=0 then∑b_jv_j lies inkerT, so equals∑a_i u_i.\n\n2. Independence of the extended basis forces allb_j and a_i zero.\n\n3. Thus Tv_j are independent and form a basis ofimT.\n\n4. Therefore dimimT=r and dimV=k+r=dimkerT+dimimT.\n\n5. If r=0 this is the empty image basis; if k=0 it states injective maps preserve domain dimension.", "role": "<p>Pull a zero combination back to the kernel.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Extended domain basis; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Rank–nullity with no finiteness requirement on W.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Rank–nullity with no finiteness requirement on W.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Extended domain basis; prior exports E1/v1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Pull a zero combination back to the kernel.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A spanning list alone cannot be counted as a basis.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum b_jTv_j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum b_jv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies inkerT, so equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Independence of the extended basis forces all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nzero.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare independent and form a basis ofimT.</p>", "<p>Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\operatorname{im} T=r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{dim} V=k+r=\\dim\\ker T+\\dim\\operatorname{im} T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis is the empty image basis; if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nit states injective maps preserve domain dimension.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A spanning list alone cannot be counted as a basis. Publish only\nafter checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A spanning list alone cannot be\ncounted as a basis. Withhold this terminal result until its gate\npasses.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Image independence and dimension", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Extended domain basis; prior exports\nE1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-extend-a-kernel-basis-1\">§4.N1 — Extend a kernel basis</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Choose a basis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nof ker T and extend it to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_k,v_{1},\\ldots ,v_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nof V.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{dim} V=k+r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in V</annotation></semantics></math>\nwrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=\\sum a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i+\\sum b_j</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>ApplyingT yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tx=\\sum b_jTv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in the kernel.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence the vectors\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nspan im T.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-image-independence-and-dimension-1\">§4.N2 — Image\nindependence and dimension</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum b_jTv_j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum b_jv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies inkerT, so equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Independence of the extended basis forces all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nzero.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Tv_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare independent and form a basis ofimT.</p></li>\n<li><p>Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\operatorname{im} T=r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{dim} V=k+r=\\dim\\ker T+\\dim\\operatorname{im} T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis is the empty image basis; if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nit states injective maps preserve domain dimension.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T:R^{3}\\to R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(x,y,z)=(x+y,z)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe kernel has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">basis(1,-1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nExtend by (0,1,0),(0,0,1); their images are (1,0),(0,1). Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3=1+2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the proof visibly constructs the image basis.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>The numerical formula uses finite dimensions. With an\ninfinite-dimensional domain one needs cardinal-dimension statements and\nappropriate basis principles; subtracting “infinite rank” from “infinite\ndimension” is not valid arithmetic. Sense keeps this studio’s\nfinite-dimensional input contract.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>The numerical formula uses finite dimensions. With an\ninfinite-dimensional domain one needs cardinal-dimension statements and\nappropriate basis principles; subtracting “infinite rank” from “infinite\ndimension” is not valid arithmetic. Sense keeps this studio’s\nfinite-dimensional input contract.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "5b49face1fbc8aad59480f17d784f323f5e62a016bdebc06daeae9b105ef539c", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of rank–nullity theorem, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/ranknullity-theorem.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/ranknullity-theorem.tex", "markdown": "markdown/ranknullity-theorem.md"}, {"id": "LA-02", "slug": "gramschmidt-orthogonalization", "title": "Gram–Schmidt Orthogonalization", "target": "<p>Given linearly independent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_1,\\ldots,v_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nin a real or complex inner-product space, prove Gram–Schmidt produces\northonormal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_1,\\ldots,q_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith equal prefix spans:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">span</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{span}(q_1,\\ldots,q_j)=\\operatorname{span}(v_1,\\ldots,v_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>The inner product is linear in its first argument and\nconjugate-linear in its second, so projection onto unit q is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle v,q\\rangle q</annotation></semantics></math>.\nGiven vectors\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{1},\\ldots ,v_k</annotation></semantics></math>\nare linearly independent. Use positivity of the norm, Pythagoras, and\nfinite induction; the ambient inner-product space may be larger or\ninfinite-dimensional.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Orthogonal residual construction", "proof": "1. Set w₁=v₁ and q₁=w₁/‖w₁‖.\n\n2. Suppose q₁,…,q_(j−1) are orthonormal with the same prefix span as the first j−1 inputs.\n\n3. Define w_j=v_j−∑_{i<j}⟨v_j,q_i⟩q_i.\n\n4. For ℓ<j, inner-product linearity gives⟨w_j,q_ℓ⟩=⟨v_j,q_ℓ⟩−⟨v_j,q_ℓ⟩=0.\n\n5. If w_j=0 then v_j is in the preceding input span, contradicting independence.\n\n6. Hence q_j=w_j/‖w_j‖ is defined and has unit norm.", "role": "<p>Remove precisely the old-span component.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Independent input vectors; existing orthonormal prefix; foundational\nimports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>Each new\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined and orthogonal to all previous\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: Each new\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined and orthogonal to all previous\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Independent input vectors; existing orthonormal prefix;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Remove precisely the old-span component.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Do not divide by a zero residual when input vectors are\ndependent.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_{1}=v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{1}=w_{1}/\\Vert w_{1}\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Suppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{1},\\ldots ,q_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nare orthonormal with the same prefix span as the first\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j-1</annotation></semantics></math>\ninputs.</p>", "<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=v_j-\\sum _{i&lt;j}\\langle v_j,q_i\\rangle q_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell &lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>,\ninner-product linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle w_j,q_\\ell \\rangle =\\langle v_j,q_\\ell \\rangle -\\langle v_j,q_\\ell \\rangle =0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis in the preceding input span, contradicting independence.</p>", "<p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j=w_j/\\Vert w_j\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined and has unit norm.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Do not divide by a zero residual when input vectors are dependent.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Do not divide by a zero residual when\ninput vectors are dependent. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Prefix-span induction", "proof": "1. The residual formula places q_j inspan(v₁,…,v_j), since earlier q_i are in the preceding span.\n\n2. Conversely v_j=‖w_j‖q_j+∑_{i<j}⟨v_j,q_i⟩q_i, so v_j belongs tospan(q₁,…,q_j).\n\n3. Earlier spans already coincide by induction.\n\n4. Thus both inclusions hold and the prefix spans agree.\n\n5. Induction completes the construction for all j; the empty input list gives an empty orthonormal list.", "role": "<p>Prove both span inclusions at every prefix.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Residual formula and nonzero normalization; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>An orthonormal list with all requested prefix-span equalities.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: An orthonormal list with all requested prefix-span\nequalities.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Residual formula and nonzero normalization; prior exports\nE1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Prove both span inclusions at every prefix.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Only the span is canonical; signs/phases and input order can change\nthe basis.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>The residual formula places\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nin span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(v_{1},\\ldots ,v_j)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince earlier\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nare in the preceding span.</p>", "<p>Conversely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=\\Vert w_j\\Vert q_j+\\sum _{i&lt;j}\\langle v_j,q_i\\rangle q_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelongs to span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(q_{1},\\ldots ,q_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Earlier spans already coincide by induction.</p>", "<p>Thus both inclusions hold and the prefix spans agree.</p>", "<p>Induction completes the construction for all j; the empty input list\ngives an empty orthonormal list.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Only the span is canonical; signs/phases and input order can change\nthe basis. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Only the span is canonical;\nsigns/phases and input order can change the basis. Withhold this\nterminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Prefix-span induction", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Residual formula and nonzero normalization;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-orthogonal-residual-construction-1\">§4.N1 — Orthogonal\nresidual construction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_{1}=v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{1}=w_{1}/\\Vert w_{1}\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Suppose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{1},\\ldots ,q_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nare orthonormal with the same prefix span as the first\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j-1</annotation></semantics></math>\ninputs.</p></li>\n<li><p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=v_j-\\sum _{i&lt;j}\\langle v_j,q_i\\rangle q_i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell &lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>,\ninner-product linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle w_j,q_\\ell \\rangle =\\langle v_j,q_\\ell \\rangle -\\langle v_j,q_\\ell \\rangle =0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis in the preceding input span, contradicting independence.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j=w_j/\\Vert w_j\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined and has unit norm.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-prefix-span-induction-1\">§4.N2 — Prefix-span induction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>The residual formula places\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nin span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(v_{1},\\ldots ,v_j)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsince earlier\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nare in the preceding span.</p></li>\n<li><p>Conversely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j=\\Vert w_j\\Vert q_j+\\sum _{i&lt;j}\\langle v_j,q_i\\rangle q_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelongs to span\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(q_{1},\\ldots ,q_j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Earlier spans already coincide by induction.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus both inclusions hold and the prefix spans agree.</p></li>\n<li><p>Induction completes the construction for all j; the empty input\nlist gives an empty orthonormal list.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{1}=(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{2}=(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{1}=(1,1)/\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe second residual is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1/2,-1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q_{2}=(1,-1)/\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth prefixes have the asserted spans, and the projection coefficient\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{2}=2v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe second residual is 0. Sense detects the failed independence\ncondition before normalization. A modified algorithm may discard\ndependent vectors and compute a basis of the span, but that is a\ndifferent output contract.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{2}=2v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe second residual is 0. Sense detects the failed independence\ncondition before normalization. A modified algorithm may discard\ndependent vectors and compute a basis of the span, but that is a\ndifferent output contract.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "32fd0a161ffbae66d34585ab777e0539b906e96d45ab40472108659db138c4da", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of gram–schmidt orthogonalization,\nwith explicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and\nreusable exports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/gramschmidt-orthogonalization.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/gramschmidt-orthogonalization.tex", "markdown": "markdown/gramschmidt-orthogonalization.md"}, {"id": "LA-03", "slug": "spectral-theorem-real-symmetric-matrices", "title": "Spectral Theorem for Real Symmetric Matrices", "target": "<p>For every real symmetric\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\times n</annotation></semantics></math>\nmatrix A, there are a real orthogonal matrix Q and a real diagonal\nmatrix Lambda such that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Q\\Lambda Q^T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p>Equivalently, Euclidean space has an orthonormal basis of\neigenvectors of A. The output includes real eigenvalues, orthogonal\neigendirections, and a reconstruction certificate. It does not claim\nuniqueness of an eigenbasis within a repeated eigenspace.</p>", "imports": ["<p>A is symmetric when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}=A</annotation></semantics></math>;\nQ is orthogonal when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^{T}Q=I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nImport compactness of the finite-dimensional unit sphere, the extreme\nvalue theorem, elementary differentiation, and induction on dimension.\nNo diagonalization theorem is imported.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Find a Maximum Without Assuming Spectral Structure", "proof": "For n≥1, the function $R(x)=x^TAx$ is continuous on the compact unit sphere. It attains a maximum at a unit vector v. Set lambda=vᵀAv, which is real. This constructs a candidate eigenvector through optimization rather than assuming one exists.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The Rayleigh quotient attains a real maximum at a unit\nvector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Symmetry and Euclidean inner product</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Study quadratic form on unit sphere</p>", "Sense": "<p>Require finite dimension and real symmetry</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Find a Maximum Without Assuming Spectral Structure. Establish the\nfollowing local result: The Rayleigh quotient attains a real maximum at\na unit vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A real symmetric\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\times n</annotation></semantics></math>\nmatrix,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncompactness of the unit sphere.</p>", "export": "<p>The Rayleigh quotient attains a real maximum at a unit vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Restrict\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^TAx</annotation></semantics></math>\nto the unit sphere.</p>", "<p>Check continuity and apply the extreme value theorem.</p>", "<p>Fix a maximizing unit vector without assuming any spectral\ndecomposition.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Require finite dimension and real symmetry Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Require finite dimension and real\nsymmetry Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Convert the Maximum into an Eigenpair", "proof": "Let w be any vector perpendicular to v, and consider\n\n$$x(t)=\\frac{v+tw}{\\sqrt{1+t^2\\|w\\|^2}}.$$\n\nThis stays on the unit sphere, x(0)=v, and x'(0)=w. Since R(x(t)) has a maximum at zero, its derivative there vanishes. Symmetry gives\n\n$$0=\\left.\\frac d{dt}x(t)^TAx(t)\\right|_{t=0}=w^TAv+v^TAw=2w^TAv.$$\n\nThus Av is orthogonal to every vector in v-perp, so Av is a multiple of v. Taking its inner product with v gives $Av=\\lambda v$. This establishes a real eigenpair for every nonzero-dimensional symmetric operator.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=\\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=v^TAv\\in\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Maximum and tangent curves</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Differentiate at maximizing point</p>", "Sense": "<p>Avoid assuming eigenvector existence</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Convert the Maximum into an Eigenpair. Establish the following local\nresult:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=\\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=v^TAv\\in\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1 and differentiable tangent curves on the sphere.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=\\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda=v^TAv\\in\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\perp v</annotation></semantics></math>,\ndifferentiate along\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(v+tw)/\\sqrt{1+t^2\\|w\\|^2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The derivative vanishes at the maximum, giving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w^TAv=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in the line spanned by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Avoid assuming eigenvector existence Publish only after checking\nevery displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Avoid assuming eigenvector existence\nRecheck dependent nodes N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Build a Smaller Symmetric Problem", "proof": "For u in v-perp,\n\n$$v^TAu=(Av)^Tu=\\lambda v^Tu=0.$$\n\nHence Au remains in v-perp: this subspace is invariant. The restricted operator is symmetric because $\\langle Au,w\\rangle=\\langle u,Aw\\rangle$ still holds for u,w there.\n\nThe restriction acts on an (n−1)-dimensional Euclidean space. The proof has now generated a smaller instance of the same theorem, with the hypotheses preserved.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the restriction there is symmetric of dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Symmetric inner-product identity</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Reduce dimension orthogonally</p>", "Sense": "<p>Restriction must remain invariant and symmetric</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Build a Smaller Symmetric Problem. Establish the following local\nresult:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the restriction there is symmetric of dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N2/E2 and symmetry of the original operator.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invariant under\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the restriction there is symmetric of dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\perp v</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncompute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle Aw,v\\rangle=\\langle w,Av\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Restrict the symmetric inner-product identity to the invariant\nsubspace.</p>", "<p>Prepare the smaller-dimensional induction problem.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Restriction must remain invariant and symmetric Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Restriction must remain invariant and\nsymmetric Recheck dependent nodes N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Induction and Reconstruction", "proof": "For n=1 the theorem is immediate. Assume it in dimension n−1. Apply it to the N3 restriction to obtain an orthonormal eigenbasis of v-perp. Adjoin v to get an orthonormal eigenbasis $v_1,\\ldots,v_n$ of the original space.\n\nLet Q have those vectors as columns and let Lambda contain their eigenvalues. Then AQ=Q Lambda and QᵀQ=I. Thus $Q^TAQ=\\Lambda$ and $A=Q\\Lambda Q^T$. This closes the induction. $\\square$\n\nAs a further consequence,\n\n$$A=\\sum_{j=1}^n\\lambda_jv_jv_j^T.$$\n\nDifferent eigenvalues have perpendicular eigenvectors: if Au=lambda u and Av=mu v, symmetry gives $(\\lambda-\\mu)u^Tv=0$. Repeated eigenvalues are handled by an orthonormal basis within their eigenspace; they do not obstruct the theorem.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Q\\Lambda Q^T</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor an orthogonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand real diagonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Lower-dimensional result</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Combine orthonormal bases</p>", "Sense": "<p>Handle repeated eigenvalues</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Induction and Reconstruction. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Q\\Lambda Q^T</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor an orthogonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand real diagonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N2/E2, N3/E3, and induction on dimension.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Q\\Lambda Q^T</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor an orthogonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand real diagonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Apply the theorem inductively on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>,\nstarting with dimension one.</p>", "<p>Join its orthonormal eigenbasis with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Check\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^TAQ=\\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the reconstruction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=\\sum_i\\lambda_i v_iv_i^T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Handle repeated eigenvalues Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Handle repeated eigenvalues Withhold\nthis terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Convert the Maximum into an Eigenpair", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1 and differentiable tangent curves on\nthe sphere.</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Build a Smaller Symmetric Problem", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2 and symmetry of the original\noperator.</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N4", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: Induction and Reconstruction", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2, N3/E3, and induction on\ndimension.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N4: Induction and Reconstruction", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2, N3/E3, and induction on\ndimension.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-find-a-maximum-without-assuming-spectral-structure-1\">N1 —\nFind a Maximum Without Assuming Spectral Structure</h3>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge 1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R(x)=x^TAx</annotation></semantics></math>\nis continuous on the compact unit sphere. It attains a maximum at a unit\nvector v. Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda =v^{T}Av</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich is real. This constructs a candidate eigenvector through\noptimization rather than assuming one exists.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n2-convert-the-maximum-into-an-eigenpair-1\">N2 — Convert the\nMaximum into an Eigenpair</h3>\n<p>Let w be any vector perpendicular to v, and consider</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(t)=\\frac{v+tw}{\\sqrt{1+t^2\\|w\\|^2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>This stays on the unit sphere,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(0)=v</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\nx’<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0)=w</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R(x(t))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a maximum at zero, its derivative there vanishes. Symmetry gives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0=\\left.\\frac d{dt}x(t)^TAx(t)\\right|_{t=0}=w^TAv+v^TAw=2w^TAv.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Thus Av is orthogonal to every vector in v-perp, so Av is a multiple\nof v. Taking its inner product with v gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=\\lambda v</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis establishes a real eigenpair for every nonzero-dimensional\nsymmetric operator.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n3-build-a-smaller-symmetric-problem-1\">N3 — Build a Smaller\nSymmetric Problem</h3>\n<p>For u in v-perp,</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v^TAu=(Av)^Tu=\\lambda v^Tu=0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Hence Au remains in v-perp: this subspace is invariant. The\nrestricted operator is symmetric because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle Au,w\\rangle=\\langle u,Aw\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>\nstill holds for u,w there.</p>\n<p>The restriction acts on an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional\nEuclidean space. The proof has now generated a smaller instance of the\nsame theorem, with the hypotheses preserved.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n4-induction-and-reconstruction-1\">N4 — Induction and\nReconstruction</h3>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe theorem is immediate. Assume it in dimension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApply it to the N3 restriction to obtain an orthonormal eigenbasis of\nv-perp. Adjoin v to get an orthonormal eigenbasis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_1,\\ldots,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nof the original space.</p>\n<p>Let Q have those vectors as columns and let Lambda contain their\neigenvalues. Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">AQ=Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nLambda and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^{T}Q=I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^TAQ=\\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=Q\\Lambda Q^T</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis closes the induction.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>▫</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>As a further consequence,</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=\\sum_{j=1}^n\\lambda_jv_jv_j^T.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Different eigenvalues have perpendicular eigenvectors: if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Au=\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nu and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av=mu</annotation></semantics></math>\nv, symmetry gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\lambda-\\mu)u^Tv=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRepeated eigenvalues are handled by an orthonormal basis within their\neigenspace; they do not obstruct the theorem.</p>", "example": "<p>Take</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0\\\\1&amp;2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0&amp;4\\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The quadratic form is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2x^2+2xy+2y^2+4z^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2xy\\le x^2+y^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3(x^2+y^2)+4z^2\\le4</annotation></semantics></math>\non the unit sphere, with equality at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nN2 therefore supplies eigenpair\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(4,e_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p>N3 restricts to the xy-plane. Its matrix is [[2,1],[1,2]], with\northonormal eigenvectors</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"></mspace><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>;</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"></mspace><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_1=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}(1,1,0),\\quad\\lambda_1=3;\\qquad v_2=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}(1,-1,0),\\quad\\lambda_2=1.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Together with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{3}=e_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand lambda\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi></mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">_{3}=4</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">diag</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q=\\begin{pmatrix}1/\\sqrt2&amp;1/\\sqrt2&amp;0\\\\1/\\sqrt2&amp;-1/\\sqrt2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\\Lambda=\\operatorname{diag}(3,1,4).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Action verifies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^{T}Q=I</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_j=\\lambda _j</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the reconstruction. The first two spectral contributions are</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3v_1v_1^T+v_2v_2^T=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1&amp;0\\\\1&amp;2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;0&amp;0\\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>while\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4v_3v_3^T</annotation></semantics></math>\nsupplies the last diagonal entry.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Symmetry is essential: [[1,1],[0,1]] has only one independent\neigenvector and cannot be diagonalized. A real rotation may have no real\neigenvalues. Positive eigenvalues are not required: symmetric matrices\ncan have negative eigenvalues. The zero matrix is covered and permits\nany orthonormal basis.</p>\n<p>Export the extremal-eigenvector lemma, invariant-complement lemma,\northogonal diagonalization, and rank-one spectral reconstruction. These\nare the exact imports used to develop singular value decomposition in\nthe problem bank.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>Suppose a branch normalizes several independently chosen eigenvectors\nand assumes they are orthogonal. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=I</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_{1}+e_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nare both eigenvectors, but normalization alone does not make them\northogonal.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Node:</strong> N4</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>State:</strong> STALLED</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failing faculty:</strong> Action</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failed claim:</strong> normalized eigenvectors form\northogonal Q</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Observed:</strong> off-diagonal entry of Q transpose Q is\nnonzero</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Repair target:</strong> basis selection</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Blocked export:</strong> orthogonal diagonalization\ncertificate</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Memory recalls orthogonal complements and repeated eigenspaces. Sense\nchecks whether the chosen vectors are independent. Intellect constructs\nan orthonormal basis in the repeated eigenspace. Action verifies its\ninner products and that every new vector remains an eigenvector. Ego\nrepublishes the decomposition only after\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q^{T}Q=I</annotation></semantics></math>\nholds.</p>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>Symmetry is essential: [[1,1],[0,1]] has only one independent\neigenvector and cannot be diagonalized. A real rotation may have no real\neigenvalues. Positive eigenvalues are not required: symmetric matrices\ncan have negative eigenvalues. The zero matrix is covered and permits\nany orthonormal basis.</p>\n<p>Export the extremal-eigenvector lemma, invariant-complement lemma,\northogonal diagonalization, and rank-one spectral reconstruction. These\nare the exact imports used to develop singular value decomposition in\nthe problem bank.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": false, "sha256": "27bd580fdb0b1ad49d880cbb9427e661967c9ece8fb18b048035dcd518a0378f", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of spectral theorem for real\nsymmetric matrices, with explicit mathematical contracts, local\nverification gates, and reusable exports.</p>", "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-700-linear-algebra-fall-2013/pages/study-materials/\">MIT\nlinear algebra: proof of the spectral theorem</a>.</p>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/spectral-theorem-real-symmetric-matrices.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/spectral-theorem-real-symmetric-matrices.tex", "markdown": "markdown/spectral-theorem-real-symmetric-matrices.md"}, {"id": "LA-04", "slug": "singular-value-decomposition", "title": "Singular Value Decomposition", "target": "<p>For every real\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\times n</annotation></semantics></math>\nmatrix\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=U\\Sigma V^T</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith orthogonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U,V</annotation></semantics></math>\nand rectangular diagonal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nhaving nonnegative singular values.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import LA-03: every real symmetric matrix has an orthonormal\neigenbasis. Import orthonormal completion from LA-02 and LA-01’s\nfinite-dimensional kernel/rank facts. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A:R^{n}\\to R^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe matrix\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>\nis symmetric positive semidefinite. U and V are square orthogonal\nmatrices;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\times n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith nonnegative entries on its rectangular diagonal.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Right singular directions", "proof": "1. Let v₁,…,v_n be an orthonormal eigenbasis of AᵀA with eigenvaluesλ_i.\n\n2. Since v_iᵀAᵀAv_i=‖Av_i‖²≥0, allλ_i≥0.\n\n3. Arrangeλ₁,…,λ_r>0 and the rest zero; putσ_i=√λ_i.\n\n4. Forλ_i=0, ‖Av_i‖²=0, so Av_i=0.\n\n5. Moreover ker(AᵀA)=kerA by this same norm identity, so r=rankA.", "role": "<p>Order positive eigenvalues before zero ones.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Spectral theorem on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>An orthonormal right basis with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_i=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: An orthonormal right basis with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_i=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Spectral theorem on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Order positive eigenvalues before zero ones.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Negative eigenvalues cannot occur; tiny computed negatives are\nnumerical errors, not theorem data.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{1},\\ldots ,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe an orthonormal eigenbasis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith eigenvalues\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i^{T}A^{T}Av_i=\\Vert Av_i\\Vert ^{2}\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nall\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Arrange\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _{1},\\ldots ,\\lambda _r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the rest zero; put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i=\\sqrt{\\lambda _i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert Av_i\\Vert ^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_i=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Moreover\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{ker} (A^{T}A)=\\operatorname{ker} A</annotation></semantics></math>\nby this same norm identity, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">rank</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=\\operatorname{rank} A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Negative eigenvalues cannot occur; tiny computed negatives are\nnumerical errors, not theorem data. Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Negative eigenvalues cannot occur;\ntiny computed negatives are numerical errors, not theorem data. Recheck\ndependent nodes N2, N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Left singular directions", "proof": "1. For i≤r define u_i=Av_i/σ_i.\n\n2. Then u_iᵀu_j=v_iᵀAᵀAv_j/(σ_iσ_j)=λ_jδ_ij/(σ_iσ_j)=δ_ij.\n\n3. Thus these r vectors are orthonormal inRᵐ, in particular r≤m.\n\n4. Complete them to an orthonormal basis u₁,…,u_m without attempting to divide zero images by zero singular values.", "role": "<p>Normalize only nonzero images.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Positive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nand right eigenvectors; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>A full orthonormal left basis whose first r vectors match positive\nsingular directions.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: A full orthonormal left basis whose first r vectors match\npositive singular directions.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Positive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nand right eigenvectors; prior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and\nversions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Normalize only nonzero images.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The zero singular values require completion, not normalization.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>\ndefine\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i/\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i^{T}u_j=v_i^{T}A^{T}Av_j/(\\sigma _i\\sigma _j)=\\lambda _j\\delta _{ij}/(\\sigma _i\\sigma _j)=\\delta _{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus these r vectors are orthonormal in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nin particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\le m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Complete them to an orthonormal basis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_m</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithout attempting to divide zero images by zero singular values.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>The zero singular values require completion, not normalization.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: The zero singular values require\ncompletion, not normalization. Recheck dependent nodes N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Factorization closure", "proof": "1. Let V have columnsv_i, U have columnsu_i, and Σ haveσ_i at(i,i) for i≤r and zeros elsewhere.\n\n2. For i≤r, UΣVᵀv_i=σ_i u_i=Av_i; for i>r both sides vanish.\n\n3. Since v_i form a basis, A=UΣVᵀ.\n\n4. This includes A=0 and rectangular dimensions.\n\n5. The sorted singular values are determined by the eigenvalues of AᵀA; bases in repeated or zero eigenspaces need not be unique.", "role": "<p>Check the equality on every basis vector.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Both orthonormal bases; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The full real rectangular SVD with nonnegative singular values.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: The full real rectangular SVD with nonnegative singular\nvalues.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Both orthonormal bases; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Check the equality on every basis vector.</p>", "Sense": "<p>No uniqueness of U or V is asserted.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Let V have columns\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nU have columns\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nat (i,i) for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zeros elsewhere.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\Sigma V^{T}v_i=\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>\nboth sides vanish.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=U\\Sigma V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This includes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand rectangular dimensions.</p>", "<p>The sorted singular values are determined by the eigenvalues of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>;\nbases in repeated or zero eigenspaces need not be unique.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>No uniqueness of U or V is asserted. Publish only after checking\nevery displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: No uniqueness of U or V is asserted.\nWithhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Left singular directions", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Positive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nand right eigenvectors; prior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Factorization closure", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Both orthonormal bases; prior exports E1/v1,\nE2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N3: Factorization closure", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Both orthonormal bases; prior exports E1/v1,\nE2/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-right-singular-directions-1\">§4.N1 — Right singular\ndirections</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_{1},\\ldots ,v_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe an orthonormal eigenbasis of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith eigenvalues\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i^{T}A^{T}Av_i=\\Vert Av_i\\Vert ^{2}\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nall\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Arrange\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _{1},\\ldots ,\\lambda _r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the rest zero; put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i=\\sqrt{\\lambda _i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda _i=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert Av_i\\Vert ^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_i=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Moreover\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{ker} (A^{T}A)=\\operatorname{ker} A</annotation></semantics></math>\nby this same norm identity, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">rank</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=\\operatorname{rank} A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-left-singular-directions-1\">§4.N2 — Left singular\ndirections</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>\ndefine\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i/\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i^{T}u_j=v_i^{T}A^{T}Av_j/(\\sigma _i\\sigma _j)=\\lambda _j\\delta _{ij}/(\\sigma _i\\sigma _j)=\\delta _{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus these r vectors are orthonormal in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nin particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\le m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Complete them to an orthonormal basis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_{1},\\ldots ,u_m</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithout attempting to divide zero images by zero singular\nvalues.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-factorization-closure-1\">§4.N3 — Factorization closure</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Let V have columns\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nU have columns\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nat (i,i) for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zeros elsewhere.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i\\le r</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\Sigma V^{T}v_i=\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>\nboth sides vanish.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nform a basis,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=U\\Sigma V^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>This includes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand rectangular dimensions.</p></li>\n<li><p>The sorted singular values are determined by the eigenvalues of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>;\nbases in repeated or zero eigenspaces need not be unique.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=[[3,0],[0,0],[0,0]]</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=I_{2},U=I_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma =A</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe singular values are 3 and 0; only the first left vector comes from\nnormalizing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Av_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe other two are an orthonormal completion.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Trying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i/\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis undefined even for the zero matrix. Sense returns that boundary test;\nMemory supplies the kernel identity, and Action completes an orthonormal\nbasis for the remaining directions.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>Trying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_i=Av_i/\\sigma _i</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma _i=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis undefined even for the zero matrix. Sense returns that boundary test;\nMemory supplies the kernel identity, and Action completes an orthonormal\nbasis for the remaining directions.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "a787eddda9fcddb5c31f0e64298c33b27d0b73aa90ed20953fd4bfc8d2ae90cf", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of singular value decomposition, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/singular-value-decomposition.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/singular-value-decomposition.tex", "markdown": "markdown/singular-value-decomposition.md"}, {"id": "LA-05", "slug": "jordan-canonical-form", "title": "Jordan Canonical Form", "target": "<p>For every complex square matrix\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=PJP^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a block-diagonal Jordan matrix\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand prove its Jordan blocks are unique up to permutation.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Work over C. Import characteristic-polynomial splitting (from the\nfundamental theorem of algebra), Cayley–Hamilton\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi _A(A)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand polynomial Bézout for coprime polynomials. Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=\\operatorname{ker} N^j</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a nilpotent restriction. The primary decomposition and\nnilpotent-chain basis are constructed below, so they are not hidden\nimports.</p>\n<p>For each nonzero primary summand let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the nilpotency index, set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{s+1}=K_s=V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFinite-dimensional basis extension and rank–nullity (LA-01) justify\ncomplement choices and dimension counts.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Primary eigenspace decomposition", "proof": "1. Set p_λ=(t−λ)^{m_λ}, P=∏p_λ and Q_λ=P/p_λ.\n\n2. Since gcd(p_λ,Q_λ)=1 choose b_λ with b_λQ_λ≡1 modp_λ.\n\n3. Put e_λ=b_λQ_λ; it is 0 modulo every other p_μ.\n\n4. Thus∑e_λ≡1 modP and e_λe_μ≡0 modP forλ≠μ.\n\n5. Evaluating atA gives projections onto V_λ=kerp_λ(A): p_λ(A)e_λ(A)=0, and e_λ(A) acts as identity on V_λ and zero on the other V_μ.\n\n6. Therefore V is their direct sum.\n\n7. On V_λ, N=A−λI is nilpotent.", "role": "<p>Construct polynomial projection operators using Bézout.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi _A(t)=\\prod _\\lambda (t-\\lambda )^{m_\\lambda }</annotation></semantics></math>;\nCayley–Hamilton; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>A direct sum of generalized eigenspaces with nilpotent\nrestrictions.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: A direct sum of generalized eigenspaces with nilpotent\nrestrictions.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\chi _A(t)=\\prod _\\lambda (t-\\lambda )^{m_\\lambda }</annotation></semantics></math>;\nCayley–Hamilton; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Construct polynomial projection operators using Bézout.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Ordinary eigenspaces alone need not span V.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda =(t-\\lambda )^{m_\\lambda }</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∏</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=\\prod p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q_\\lambda =P/p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">gcd</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{gcd} (p_\\lambda ,Q_\\lambda )=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_\\lambda Q_\\lambda \\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda =b_\\lambda Q_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nit is 0 modulo every other\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum e_\\lambda \\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod P and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda e_\\mu \\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod P for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda \\ne \\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Evaluating at A gives projections onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda =\\operatorname{ker}</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda (A)</annotation></semantics></math>:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda (A)e_\\lambda (A)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda (A)</annotation></semantics></math>\nacts as identity on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zero on the other\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Therefore V is their direct sum.</p>", "<p>On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=A-\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nilpotent.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Ordinary eigenspaces alone need not span V. Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Ordinary eigenspaces alone need not\nspan V. Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Choose chain heads from the kernel filtration", "proof": "1. For each j=1,…,s choose a subspace W_j complementary to K_(j−1)+N K_(j+1) in K_j.\n\n2. The denominator lies inK_j.\n\n3. Its intersection K_(j−1)∩N K_(j+1) equalsN K_j: if Nz lies inK_(j−1), N^jz=0 so z∈K_j.\n\n4. Writing d_j=dimK_j and d₀=0,d_(s+1)=d_s, and using dimN K_j=d_j−d₁, gives w_j=dimW_j=2d_j−d_(j−1)−d_(j+1).\n\n5. A nonzero chosen basis vector inW_j does not lie inK_(j−1), so its N-chain has exact lengthj.", "role": "<p>Complement the lower layer plus images of longer chains.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Nilpotent N with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_s=V</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{s+1}=V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Chain heads of exact lengths j, with counts\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Chain heads of exact lengths j, with counts\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Nilpotent N with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_s=V</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{s+1}=V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Complement the lower layer plus images of longer chains.</p>", "Sense": "<p>An arbitrary basis of kerN cannot serve as chain heads for all\nlengths.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=1,\\ldots ,s</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose a subspace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_j</annotation></semantics></math>\ncomplementary to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}+N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The denominator lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Its intersection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}\\cap N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nequals N\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>:\nif Nz lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N^jz=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Writing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_j=\\operatorname{dim} K_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{0}=0,d_{s+1}=d_s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand using dimN\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=d_j-d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=\\operatorname{dim} W_j=2d_j-d_{j-1}-d_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>A nonzero chosen basis vector in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_j</annotation></semantics></math>\ndoes not lie in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso its N-chain has exact lengthj.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>An arbitrary basis of kerN cannot serve as chain heads for all\nlengths. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: An arbitrary basis of kerN cannot\nserve as chain heads for all lengths. Recheck dependent nodes N3,\nN4.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Prove the chains form a basis", "proof": "1. The identity K_j=K_(j−1)+W_j+N K_(j+1) can be expanded upwards.\n\n2. Terms N K_j lie inK_(j−1), giving K_j⊂K_(j−1)+∑_{ℓ=j}^s N^{ℓ−j}W_ℓ.\n\n3. Descend through j=s,…,1; this shows all ofV is spanned by the chains w,Nw,…,N^{j−1}w for basis headsw∈W_j.\n\n4. Their total number is∑_{j=1}^s j w_j=∑j(2d_j−d_(j−1)−d_(j+1))=d_s by telescoping.\n\n5. A spanning list of exactly dimV vectors is a basis.\n\n6. Order each chain as(N^{j−1}w,…,Nw,w); N then has ones on the superdiagonal and zeros elsewhere in that block.", "role": "<p>Show spanning and count exactly dimV vectors.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Complement identities for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>A basis of nilpotent Jordan chains on each generalized\neigenspace.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: A basis of nilpotent Jordan chains on each generalized\neigenspace.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Complement identities for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Show spanning and count exactly dimV vectors.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Both spanning and exact count are needed; a collection of chains may\notherwise be dependent.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>The identity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=K_{j-1}+W_j+N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncan be expanded upwards.</p>", "<p>Terms N\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nlie in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j\\subset K_{j-1}+\\sum _{\\ell =j}^s</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N^{\\ell -j}W_\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Descend through\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=s,\\ldots ,1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthis shows all of V is spanned by the chains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w,Nw,\\ldots ,N^{j-1}w</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor basis heads\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in W_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Their total number is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum _{j=1}^s</annotation></semantics></math>\nj\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=\\sum j(2d_j-d_{j-1}-d_{j+1})=d_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nby telescoping.</p>", "<p>A spanning list of exactly dimV vectors is a basis.</p>", "<p>Order each chain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">as(N^{j-1}w,\\ldots ,Nw,w)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nN then has ones on the superdiagonal and zeros elsewhere in that\nblock.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Both spanning and exact count are needed; a collection of chains may\notherwise be dependent. Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Both spanning and exact count are\nneeded; a collection of chains may otherwise be dependent. Recheck\ndependent nodes N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Jordan form and block uniqueness", "proof": "1. Joining the bases over distinctλ gives J with blocks J_j(λ), so A=PJP⁻¹ for the change-of-basis matrixP.\n\n2. A lengthℓ block contributes min(j,ℓ) to dimkerN^j.\n\n3. Thus d_j−d_(j−1) is the number of blocks of length at leastj, and w_j=(d_j−d_(j−1))−(d_(j+1)−d_j) is the number of length exactlyj.\n\n4. These kernel dimensions are invariant under similarity, as are the eigenvalues.\n\n5. Hence every block multiplicity is determined, proving uniqueness up to block order.", "role": "<p>Read block multiplicities from invariant kernel dimensions.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Chain bases in all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1, E3/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Existence and uniqueness up to permutation of complex Jordan\nblocks.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1: Existence and uniqueness up to permutation of complex\nJordan blocks.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Chain bases in all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1, E3/v1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Read block multiplicities from invariant kernel dimensions.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Uniqueness concerns block data, not the chain basis or\nchange-of-basis matrix.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Joining the bases over distinct\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives J with blocks\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J_j(\\lambda )</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=PJP</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi></mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the change-of-basis matrix P.</p>", "<p>A length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>\nblock contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{min} (j,\\ell )</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\ker N^j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_j-d_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the number of blocks of length at leastj, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=(d_j-d_{j-1})-(d_{j+1}-d_j)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the number of length exactlyj.</p>", "<p>These kernel dimensions are invariant under similarity, as are the\neigenvalues.</p>", "<p>Hence every block multiplicity is determined, proving uniqueness up\nto block order.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Uniqueness concerns block data, not the chain basis or\nchange-of-basis matrix. Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Uniqueness concerns block data, not\nthe chain basis or change-of-basis matrix. Withhold this terminal result\nuntil its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Choose chain heads from the kernel filtration", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Nilpotent N with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_s=V</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{s+1}=V</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Prove the chains form a basis", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Complement identities for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N4", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: Jordan form and block uniqueness", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Chain bases in all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1, E3/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N4", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N4: Jordan form and block uniqueness", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Chain bases in all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1, E3/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T5", "activity": "N4: Jordan form and block uniqueness", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Chain bases in all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1, E3/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-primary-eigenspace-decomposition-1\">§4.N1 — Primary\neigenspace decomposition</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda =(t-\\lambda )^{m_\\lambda }</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∏</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P=\\prod p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q_\\lambda =P/p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">gcd</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{gcd} (p_\\lambda ,Q_\\lambda )=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_\\lambda Q_\\lambda \\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda =b_\\lambda Q_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>;\nit is 0 modulo every other\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum e_\\lambda \\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod P and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda e_\\mu \\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod P for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda \\ne \\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Evaluating at A gives projections onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda =\\operatorname{ker}</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda (A)</annotation></semantics></math>:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_\\lambda (A)e_\\lambda (A)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_\\lambda (A)</annotation></semantics></math>\nacts as identity on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\nand zero on the other\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Therefore V is their direct sum.</p></li>\n<li><p>On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=A-\\lambda I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nilpotent.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-choose-chain-heads-from-the-kernel-filtration-1\">§4.N2 —\nChoose chain heads from the kernel filtration</h3>\n<p>On a primary summand let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the nilpotency index,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=\\ker N^j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{s+1}=K_s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=1,\\ldots ,s</annotation></semantics></math>\nchoose a subspace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_j</annotation></semantics></math>\ncomplementary to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}+N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The denominator lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its intersection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}\\cap N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nequals N\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>:\nif Nz lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N^jz=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in K_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Writing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_j=\\operatorname{dim} K_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{0}=0,d_{s+1}=d_s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand using dimN\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=d_j-d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=\\operatorname{dim} W_j=2d_j-d_{j-1}-d_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>A nonzero chosen basis vector in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_j</annotation></semantics></math>\ndoes not lie in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso its N-chain has exact lengthj.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-prove-the-chains-form-a-basis-1\">§4.N3 — Prove the chains\nform a basis</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>The identity\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j=K_{j-1}+W_j+N</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncan be expanded upwards.</p></li>\n<li><p>Terms N\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nlie in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ngiving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_j\\subset K_{j-1}+\\sum _{\\ell =j}^s</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N^{\\ell -j}W_\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Descend through\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=s,\\ldots ,1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthis shows all of V is spanned by the chains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w,Nw,\\ldots ,N^{j-1}w</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor basis heads\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in W_j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Their total number is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum _{j=1}^s</annotation></semantics></math>\nj\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=\\sum j(2d_j-d_{j-1}-d_{j+1})=d_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nby telescoping.</p></li>\n<li><p>A spanning list of exactly dimV vectors is a basis.</p></li>\n<li><p>Order each chain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">as(N^{j-1}w,\\ldots ,Nw,w)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nN then has ones on the superdiagonal and zeros elsewhere in that\nblock.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n4-jordan-form-and-block-uniqueness-1\">§4.N4 — Jordan form and\nblock uniqueness</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Joining the bases over distinct\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives J with blocks\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J_j(\\lambda )</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=PJP</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi></mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the change-of-basis matrix P.</p></li>\n<li><p>A length\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>\nblock contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{min} (j,\\ell )</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dim\\ker N^j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_j-d_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the number of blocks of length at leastj, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_j=(d_j-d_{j-1})-(d_{j+1}-d_j)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the number of length exactlyj.</p></li>\n<li><p>These kernel dimensions are invariant under similarity, as are\nthe eigenvalues.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence every block multiplicity is determined, proving uniqueness\nup to block order.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For a nilpotent operator with kernel dimensions\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{1}=2,d_{2}=3,d_{3}=4</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{4}=4</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe increments are 2,1,1,0. There are two blocks total, one of length 3\nand one of length 1. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J=J_{3}(0)\\oplus J_{1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand no block of length 2 occurs.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Over R a rotation matrix has no real eigenvalue, so a real Jordan\nmatrix with real diagonal entries cannot represent it. Sense keeps the\ncomplex-field contract; a real canonical form needs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">separate2\\times 2</annotation></semantics></math>\nblocks for conjugate eigenvalues.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>Over R a rotation matrix has no real eigenvalue, so a real Jordan\nmatrix with real diagonal entries cannot represent it. Sense keeps the\ncomplex-field contract; a real canonical form needs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">separate2\\times 2</annotation></semantics></math>\nblocks for conjugate eigenvalues.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "299eecdf9da4649c921935484a8216061653ee92572b5b48bd8efab7b35131f8", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of jordan canonical form, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-18-012-algebra-ii-student-notes-spring-2022/pages/student-notes/\">MIT\nAlgebra II notes: field extensions and Galois theory</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/jordan-canonical-form.pdf", "tex": "reports/latex/jordan-canonical-form.tex", "markdown": "markdown/jordan-canonical-form.md"}], "links": [{"source": "LA-01", "target": "LA-04", "label": "Rank and kernel", "detail": "The equality of the two kernels identifies the number of positive singular values."}, {"source": "LA-02", "target": "LA-04", "label": "Orthonormal completion", "detail": "The nonzero left singular vectors extend to a full orthonormal basis."}, {"source": "LA-03", "target": "LA-04", "label": "Spectral theorem", "detail": "The symmetric positive semidefinite matrix AᵀA has an orthonormal eigenbasis."}, {"source": "LA-01", "target": "LA-05", "label": "Kernel dimensions", "detail": "Dimension counting proves the chain basis and recovers block multiplicities."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs. No deployed agent execution or formal kernel verification is claimed."};
